WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.979
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Cambridge exams.

2
00:00:05.279 --> 00:00:09.037
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.337 --> 00:00:16.099
Unit five: A2 Key: Speaking. Today you will answer personal questions and talk about pictures with a partner.

4
00:00:16.399 --> 00:00:19.040
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.453
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.317 --> 00:00:25.155
Partner.

7
00:00:26.150 --> 00:00:28.440
Partner means the other student in the exam.

8
00:00:29.050 --> 00:00:30.515
Talk with your partner.

9
00:00:31.117 --> 00:00:33.769
Your turn. Say: Partner.

10
00:00:36.633 --> 00:00:37.402
Partner.

11
00:00:38.150 --> 00:00:39.314
Examiner.

12
00:00:40.317 --> 00:00:43.152
Examiner means the person who asks questions.

13
00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:45.424
The examiner is friendly.

14
00:00:46.017 --> 00:00:48.878
Your turn. Say: Examiner.

15
00:00:51.733 --> 00:00:52.862
Examiner.

16
00:00:53.617 --> 00:00:54.734
Introduce.

17
00:00:55.750 --> 00:00:57.854
Introduce means to say who you are.

18
00:00:58.450 --> 00:00:59.811
Introduce yourself.

19
00:01:00.417 --> 00:01:02.930
Your turn. Say: Introduce.

20
00:01:05.767 --> 00:01:06.965
Introduce.

21
00:01:07.717 --> 00:01:08.636
Favourite.

22
00:01:09.650 --> 00:01:11.429
Favourite means liked best.

23
00:01:12.017 --> 00:01:13.900
My favourite food is rice.

24
00:01:14.517 --> 00:01:16.856
Your turn. Say: Favourite.

25
00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:20.562
Favourite.

26
00:01:21.317 --> 00:01:22.283
Routine.

27
00:01:23.283 --> 00:01:26.096
Routine means your usual daily activities.

28
00:01:26.683 --> 00:01:28.149
My routine is simple.

29
00:01:28.750 --> 00:01:31.170
Your turn. Say: Routine.

30
00:01:34.033 --> 00:01:35.023
Routine.

31
00:01:35.783 --> 00:01:37.249
Ask for repetition.

32
00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:41.527
Ask for repetition means to ask someone to say it again.

33
00:01:42.117 --> 00:01:43.443
Could you say that again?

34
00:01:44.050 --> 00:01:47.236
Your turn. Say: Ask for repetition.

35
00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:51.658
Ask for repetition.

36
00:01:52.417 --> 00:01:53.476
Prompt card.

37
00:01:54.483 --> 00:01:57.400
Prompt card means a card with pictures to talk about.

38
00:01:58.017 --> 00:01:59.540
Use the prompt cards.

39
00:02:00.150 --> 00:02:02.721
Your turn. Say: Prompt card.

40
00:02:05.567 --> 00:02:06.846
Prompt card.

41
00:02:07.583 --> 00:02:08.329
Reason.

42
00:02:09.317 --> 00:02:10.782
Reason means why.

43
00:02:11.383 --> 00:02:12.431
Give a reason.

44
00:02:13.017 --> 00:02:15.193
Your turn. Say: Reason.

45
00:02:18.033 --> 00:02:18.883
Reason.

46
00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:24.129
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:24.983 --> 00:02:27.505
Visal, what happens in A2 Key Speaking?

48
00:02:28.617 --> 00:02:39.826
You take the exam with another student and two examiners. First you answer questions about yourself, then you ask and answer questions with your partner using cards.

49
00:02:40.917 --> 00:02:42.672
How can I show good English?

50
00:02:43.783 --> 00:02:53.242
Answer with more than one word. Say, I like football because it is exciting, instead of just Yes. Speak clearly and listen to your partner.

51
00:02:54.350 --> 00:02:56.141
What if I do not understand?

52
00:02:57.250 --> 00:03:04.407
Say, Sorry, could you say that again? That is natural and polite, and examiners are happy to repeat.

53
00:03:05.567 --> 00:03:07.206
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:08.050 --> 00:03:12.488
Grammar focus: Strategy: full answers and polite questions.

55
00:03:12.788 --> 00:03:14.056
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:14.750 --> 00:03:16.924
I like football because it is exciting.

57
00:03:17.817 --> 00:03:19.572
Sorry, could you say that again?

58
00:03:20.533 --> 00:03:28.111
Answer with full sentences and a reason. If you do not understand, ask politely. Listen to your partner and keep the conversation going.

59
00:03:28.850 --> 00:03:32.176
Be careful! Don't say: I answer with one word.

60
00:03:34.133 --> 00:03:36.597
Say: I answer with a full sentence.

61
00:03:36.897 --> 00:03:38.049
Give a reason.

62
00:03:38.833 --> 00:03:41.671
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:42.467 --> 00:03:44.141
A Speaking Practice.

64
00:03:44.441 --> 00:03:46.406
Chhay practises with a friend.

65
00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:49.818
The friend asks what he does after school.

66
00:03:50.833 --> 00:03:53.901
Chhay answers that he plays football because it is exciting.

67
00:03:54.900 --> 00:03:57.341
Then he asks his friend the same question.

68
00:03:58.333 --> 00:04:01.320
He asks politely when he does not understand a word.

69
00:04:02.433 --> 00:04:06.273
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:07.117 --> 00:04:08.965
In Speaking you work with blank.

71
00:04:09.265 --> 00:04:13.081
A, nobody. B, a dog. C, a partner.

72
00:04:16.633 --> 00:04:18.273
The answer is C: a partner.

73
00:04:19.417 --> 00:04:20.975
A good answer is blank.

74
00:04:21.275 --> 00:04:25.915
A, more than one word. B, only yes. C, silence.

75
00:04:29.467 --> 00:04:31.838
The answer is A: more than one word.

76
00:04:32.983 --> 00:04:35.122
What does Chhay do after school?

77
00:04:35.422 --> 00:04:39.668
A, studies maths. B, plays football. C, sleeps.

78
00:04:43.233 --> 00:04:45.477
The answer is B: plays football.

79
00:04:46.617 --> 00:04:48.837
What do you say if you do not understand?

80
00:04:49.137 --> 00:04:53.080
A, Nothing. B, Goodbye. C, Could you say that again?.

81
00:04:56.633 --> 00:04:59.179
The answer is C: Could you say that again?.

82
00:05:00.317 --> 00:05:02.003
Why is football exciting?

83
00:05:02.303 --> 00:05:06.165
A, it is exciting. B, it is cheap. C, it is old.

84
00:05:09.700 --> 00:05:11.932
The answer is A: it is exciting.

85
00:05:13.133 --> 00:05:16.169
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:17.017 --> 00:05:19.492
Tell me about yourself and what you do after school.

87
00:05:28.283 --> 00:05:29.691
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:29.991 --> 00:05:41.702
My name is Chhay, and I am fourteen. After school I play football with my friends because it is exciting. On weekends I help my family at home and watch films.

89
00:05:42.002 --> 00:05:43.769
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:44.683 --> 00:05:50.784
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: full answers and polite questions.

91
00:05:51.084 --> 00:05:55.083
Today's value is confidence. Speak up and be proud of who you are.

92
00:05:55.383 --> 00:05:57.884
See you in Unit six. Goodbye!

93
00:05:58.184 --> 00:06:00.790
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

